# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database connections. .env is gitignored (.gitignore: `.env*`) — do not commit.
#
# Two roles by design (see docs/schema.sql §RLS and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7f):
#
#  • DATABASE_URL  → `stack`  — the least-privileged runtime role. NOSUPERUSER,
#    NOBYPASSRLS. The app/service layer connects as this and Row-Level Security is
#    ENFORCED, so every query is confined to the active tenant. The service layer
#    MUST open each request/transaction with:
#        SET LOCAL app.current_company_id = '<uuid>';
#        SET LOCAL app.current_user_id    = '<uuid>';
#    (see src/lib/prisma.ts → withTenant()).
#
#  • DIRECT_URL    → `postgres` — owner/superuser. Used ONLY by the Prisma CLI
#    (db pull / migrate / studio) for schema management; it bypasses RLS. The
#    running app never uses this. prisma.config.ts points the CLI at DIRECT_URL.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

DATABASE_URL=""
DIRECT_URL=""

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auth. JWT session tokens (jose, HS256) stored in an httpOnly cookie.
# AUTH_SECRET signs/verifies them — rotating it invalidates all sessions.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AUTH_SECRET=""
